Auloud Player, full flavor: license note (D-126 option A).

[Owner-confirmed 2026-10-10, with NOTICE.full and the filled
SOURCE_OFFER.txt. The full flavor may ship.]

The sherpa-carrying `full` flavor is distributed as a GPL-3.0 combined
work, not under the Apache-2.0 LICENSE in this directory (that file
covers the Player source and the `core` flavor):

- App code: Apache-2.0 (this directory's LICENSE), included in the
  GPL-3.0 work as the GPL permits.
- sherpa-onnx 1.13.8 (JitPack AAR, Apache-2.0 POM): bundled speech
  runtime; its native libraries include statically linked espeak-ng
  (GPL-3.0-or-later), which is what makes the distributed full APK a
  GPL-3.0 combined work.
- onnxruntime native library (MIT): bundled inside the sherpa AAR.

The full APK carries the GPL-3.0 license text
(player/app/src/full/assets/gpl-3.0.txt), the written source offer
(player/app/src/full/assets/SOURCE_OFFER.txt), and the full notice
(player/app/src/full/assets/NOTICE.txt). The per-flavor dependency
list is player/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.full.md; the in-app list under
Settings > Licenses matches it.

Build the flavors from player/ with:
gradlew.bat :app:assembleCoreRelease (main Apache-2.0 release)
gradlew.bat :app:assembleFullRelease (GPL-3.0 combined work)
Verify with:
gradlew.bat :app:assembleCoreDebug :app:assembleFullDebug :app:licenseScan

This is not legal advice.
